<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">River Deveron</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Deveron</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The River Deveron is a river in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, flowing about 100 kilometres from the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberdeenshire">Aberdeenshire</a> past Huntly and Turriff to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> at Banff and Macduff. Its valley formed part of the fertile lowland of the Taexali in the Roman period. It is known today for its salmon and sea trout fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/river-deveron.jpg" alt="River Deveron" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anne Burgess · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_Deveron_Near_Inverkeithny_-_geograph.org.uk_-_990270.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
